# backend/.dockerignore
#
# NOTE on why this file exists here vs. at the project root: Docker
# resolves ignore files two ways for `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .`
# (context = project root):
#   1. A Dockerfile-specific file co-located with the Dockerfile and named
#      after it: backend/Dockerfile.dockerignore (BuildKit only).
#   2. Falls back to a plain .dockerignore at the CONTEXT ROOT (project
#      root) if #1 doesn't exist.
# This file is kept here as backend/.dockerignore per how it was asked
# for, and doubles as the source of truth — but Docker itself won't pick
# up a file at this exact path/name automatically. The project root's
# .dockerignore (kept in sync with this one) is what Docker actually
# reads for the build in this repo. Rename this file to
# backend/Dockerfile.dockerignore instead if you'd rather rely on
# BuildKit's Dockerfile-specific convention (option 1) than the root
# fallback (option 2) — either works, just keep only one in sync.

# Secrets / environment
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Tests
tests/
test_*.py
*_test.py

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Local databases (sqlite dev fallback — never ship into the image)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Generated report output (regenerated at runtime)
frontend/static/reports/output/
*.pdf

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Windows dev-only scripts — irrelevant inside a Linux container
*.ps1
*.bat

# Docs not needed at runtime
README.md
